out/hang degradation cause; the degradation-cause test tier covers only empty-PAT and ConfigError."],"finding":"The bounded-timeout mechanism for the live probe is committed to in intent but its location is left open ('S8's build_probe transport, or wrapped here'), deferring a reliability-relevant implementation choice to the executor without a stated default.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc88d9d3852b4920a","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — Live-drift check, parenthetical on bounded timeout","norm_id":"na13a29f0aa9d4013","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A slow/hanging Data Center host during a doctor run"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Pick one location as the default (e.g. 'wrap the probe call in a bounded timeout here') and add a transport-raise/timeout case to the degradation-cause unit tier asserting it folds into one `unavailable` finding + success exit.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Correct the timeout premise: S8's build_probe/build_client_from_settings sets no request timeout, so specify the 'wrapped here' bounded-timeout wrapper (where it lives, its bound, and how the transport-timeout cause folds into the single `unavailable` finding) rather than attributing the bound to S8's transport.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.15,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["mapping_probe.build_probe (mapping_probe.py:195-211) calls build_client_from_settings and returns _JiraProbePort — no timeout wrapper","adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py:155-199 build_client_from_settings constructs jira.JIRA with server/token_auth/options only — no timeout kwarg or option","search_files for 'timeout' across adapters/jira_datacenter/ returns only retry.py comments about read-timeout classification, no configured request timeout","Scope/Testing explicitly treat the transport path as S8-covered / not-applicable ('treats the real-transport path as explicitly not-applicable'), so the timeout-degradation cause is not tested in this child"],"finding":"The plan asserts the live-drift probe 'runs under a bounded timeout — S8's build_probe transport', but S8's build_client_from_settings sets no timeout on the jira.JIRA client (no 'timeout' anywhere in adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py or the package), so a slow/hanging Data Center host is NOT bounded by the reused transport as claimed.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f36a67e45a44aa7ac","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Live-drift check ('the probe runs under a bounded timeout — S8's build_probe transport, or wrapped here — so a slow/hanging Data Center host degrades not blocks')","norm_id":"n28d5d5fe5bc8eeef","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reachable-but-hanging DC host during `rebar doctor`: with no bounded timeout in the reused transport, the probe blocks instead of degrading to the single `unavailable` finding the plan promises"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Drop the 'S8's build_probe transport' clause and instead commit to a doctor-side bounded-timeout wrapper around the probe call (e.g. a thread/future with a timeout, or passing a timeout into the jira client), and add a degradation-cause test that drives a hanging/slow probe to the `unavailable` finding.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Split the offline check into (a) a guarded load_mapping_config() call catching load-time MappingConfigError (non-integer hierarchy, malformed block) into an error finding whose key is recovered from the error's `where` path, and (b) the per-key resolver pass for resolve-time errors (out-of-vocabulary, unmapped-non-skipped type) — rather than framing all three error-classes as produced by one per-key enumeration.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2889,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Load the MappingConfig once, then enumerate every configured key in config.projects union the default layer, running the resolvers per key so per-project errors are actually reached and named.'","mapping_config.py:161-164 (_parse_hierarchy) raises MappingConfigError for a non-integer rank; mapping_config.py:169-202 (_parse_layer) raises for a malformed block — both invoked inside load_mapping_config (mapping_config.py:205-230), i.e. at LOAD, before config.projects exists.","Only out-of-vocabulary (validate / _check_vocab, mapping_config.py:307-359) and unmapped-non-skipped-type (config.assert_type_decisions_complete, config.py:178-209) surface at RESOLVE time — so the per-key resolver loop reaches only one of the three error-classes.","AC-2 asserts the non-integer-hierarchy finding is produced by 'the offline check enumerates config.projects + the default layer per key' — an enumeration that is structurally unreachable when the load raises first."],"finding":"The offline check's stated control-flow ('load MappingConfig once, then enumerate config.projects + default per key, running resolvers per key so per-project errors are reached and named') cannot reach the enumeration for two of its three named error-classes, because non-integer hierarchy and malformed-block errors are raised inside load_mapping_config itself — before config.projects is available to iterate.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f54147145d9819ec4","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → 'Offline checks (always run...)'; Acceptance Criteria line 2 (offline error-class AC)","norm_id":"n13a656653faa0499","priority":0.8889,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A [mapping.projects.PROJ.hierarchy] block with a string rank value: load_mapping_config raises before any per-key enumeration; without a separate guard the whole doctor invocation raises instead of emitting an error finding.","A [mapping.default] block that is not a table (malformed): same load-time raise."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Wrap the initial load_mapping_config() in try/except MappingConfigError: on catch, emit one error finding (the message already carries the key via its `where=` path, e.g. 'projects.PROJ.hierarchy') and skip the per-key pass; only when the load succeeds enumerate config.projects + the default layer and run effective_status_map / effective_type_map / assert_type_decisions_complete / effective_link_map per key to reach the resolve-time error-classes.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Resolve the bounded-timeout mechanism the 'degrades not blocks' guarantee depends on: either confirm build_probe's transport already imposes a per-request timeout (cite it) or specify the 'wrapped here' bound (e.g., a timeout applied around the probe call), and add a degradation-cause test for a hanging/slow-transport probe rather than deferring the whole transport cause to S8.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.0,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'the probe transport raises or times out (the probe runs under a bounded timeout — S8's build_probe transport, or wrapped here — so a slow/hanging Data Center host degrades not blocks)'","transport.py build_client_from_settings: `return jira_cls(server=settings.url, token_auth=settings.pat, options=options or None)` — no timeout passed","search for 'timeout' under adapters/jira_datacenter finds only retry.py comments about retrying a socket read-timeout, not a configured request timeout on the probe path","resolve_symbol: jira.JIRA EXISTS; pycontribs/jira uses timeout=None by default (no client-side timeout) — Partially-verified: the integration exists but the specific bounded-timeout surface is unconfirmed/absent","Testing section drives only 'each non-transport cause' for degradation; the transport hang/timeout cause is deferred to S8 and not exercised here"],"finding":"The plan asserts the live-drift probe 'runs under a bounded timeout — S8's build_probe transport, or wrapped here — so a slow/hanging Data Center host degrades not blocks', but the reused S8 transport does not impose a client-side timeout: build_client_from_settings constructs jira.JIRA(server=..., token_auth=..., options=...) with no timeout, and pycontribs/jira defaults to no request timeout. The jira_datacenter retry.py only retries a read-timeout the socket/server actually raises; it does not bound a genuinely hanging connect/read. So the 'degrades not blocks' guarantee for a hanging host is unverified in the reused code, and the plan's own 'or wrapped here' hedge leaves the mechanism unspecified.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fcde11ec5cb1d3df8","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach → Live-drift check bullet ('the probe runs under a bounded timeout — S8's build_probe transport, or wrapped here')","norm_id":"ncceb5928a2e330b6","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Doctor is run with the jira-datacenter extra installed and credentials set against a DC host that accepts the TCP connection but never responds (silent-drop firewall / overloaded instance) — the probe blocks indefinitely instead of emitting the promised single 'unavailable' finding"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Since build_client_from_settings sets no timeout, specify the 'wrapped here' path concretely — e.g., run the probe under an explicit bounded wall-clock bound in the doctor check and fold a timeout into the single 'unavailable' finding — and cover it with a fake-probe test whose reader sleeps/raises a timeout, asserting one 'unavailable' finding + success exit.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}}],"impact_model_version":"plan-v5","material_fingerprint":"a71798f893bfed83","material_parts":{"children":["647ea2107ca5072f",0],"description":["7d7f12a6dae46b24",7993],"description_boxes":["90a512a5b8a10706",0],"file_impact":["6ab6b236391b8bd5",3],"ticket_id":["297f2969fb7ae9ac",19]},"metrics":{"cache_read_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"claim_path":"no-llm/no-network (structural; the fast claim check is a local HMAC verify)","det_ms":4378.0,"input_tokens":1668962,"llm_calls":29,"llm_ms":285413.5,"output_tokens":30381,"precheck":{"cited_anchor_warning":false},"total_ms":301862.0,"verify_requests":10},"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","provider_provenance":{"candidates":["bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6"],"capabilities":{"native_structured_output":true,"prompt_cache_style":"none","supports_temperature":true,"supports_thinking":true,"web_access":"off"},"endpoint_host":null,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","provider":"bedrock","ran_model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","region":"us-east-1","region_source":"REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION","tier":"first_class"},"regver":"362a5dd2d2052826","review_phase":"planning","reviewed_related_material":[{"canonical_id":"ad81-73ad-83bb-47c7","material_fingerprint":"8d7277191711d8b8","role":"prerequisite"},{"canonical_id":"bfe7-0900-c3d1-4141","material_fingerprint":"2814cef81e53ef63","role":"prerequisite"}],"runner":"pydantic_ai","schema":"plan_review_result_v2","source":"attested","ticket_id":"52b0-6a6a-c66b-4c59","ticket_type":"story","verdict":"BLOCK","verified_at_sha":"9c1c66c59bf1e893f94f699cfda903a3b3c80748"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"REVIEW_RESULT","timestamp":1787390889583707001,"uuid":"3cec76e1-1866-43ef-869e-004641581b5f"}